   "acf984517dbb6370c640a8d1fced94ddbc6799b86041746791959246da90c972",
   :after
   "Executed startup/failure/resource fixtures and manifest-to-service agreement. R1/R3/R4: typed host adapters with effects, capabilities, taint, error and source-map contracts; selected host/version/module/collection/dynamic-state manifests; startup, initialization, handoff and teardown order; explicit panic/trap/abort/unwind/result policy; host null/undefined conversion, exception and rejected-promise translation; Gravity equality/hashing/serialization conformance; deterministic linear cleanup independent of process exit or GC. Reject undeclared helper effects, untranslated/null foreign values and GC-only linear cleanup; debug services must be absent or release-policy marked. Dependencies: Lower supplies ABI and source maps, Legality supplies legal services, and Auth supplies grants; selected compiler services do not close all managed/native targets.",
   :id
   "runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/finish-managednative-execution-startup-panic-and-cleanup",
   :before
   "Executed startup/failure/resource fixtures and manifest-to-service agreement",
   :collection :canonical-tasks}
  {:path "specs/runtime-workflow/tasks.md",
   :before-present? true,
   :field-path [:acceptance],
   :marker "runtime-implementation-tasks",
   :after-source-sha256
   "221b129f96156493c03e73e0ef3e8987f50425fcb15925c6a229144ea54539a1",
   :before-source-sha256
   "acf984517dbb6370c640a8d1fced94ddbc6799b86041746791959246da90c972",
   :after
   "Allocation, lifetime, transfer, race and foreign-failure conformance with explicit providers. R3/R5/R6/R10: allocation/deallocation/provider manifests, no-allocation and region/arena escape rejection, linear acquire/transfer/consume ledgers, device address-space/transfer/synchronization/lifetime checks, audited raw-memory wrappers, and agreement of retained checks with exact proof-elision records; atomics with target memory order/scope/alignment, structured task parent or explicit lifecycle owner, cancellation cleanup and failure propagation, actor/channel schemas with ordering/backpressure/transfer policy; FFI symbol/loading policy, ABI/layout conformance, null/handle/lifetime/ownership/error adapters and callbacks re-entering capability/taint/thread-affinity/scheduler checks. Reject mismatched providers, races, orphan tasks, unsupported atomics, schemaless messages, raw extern safe calls and invalid callback entry. Dependencies: ownership and Legality supply compile-time facts, Lower supplies target layouts, Auth supplies grants, and distributed execution supplies replay policy; runtime debug checks cannot substitute for compile-time safety.",
   :id
   "runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries",
   :before
   "Allocation, lifetime, transfer, race and foreign-failure conformance with explicit providers",
   :collection :canonical-tasks}
  {:path "specs/runtime-workflow/tasks.md",
   :before-present? true,
   :field-path [:acceptance],
   :marker "runtime-implementation-tasks",
   :after-source-sha256
   "221b129f96156493c03e73e0ef3e8987f50425fcb15925c6a229144ea54539a1",
   :before-source-sha256
   "acf984517dbb6370c640a8d1fced94ddbc6799b86041746791959246da90c972",
   :after
   "Recorded nondeterminism, replay equality, no duplicated external effect, REPL grant denial. R6/R7/R8/R9: topology/provider/event-log/state/message schemas; durable idempotency, timeout/retry/cancellation/failure/compensation records; migration or rejection of replay-incompatible code/topology/schema changes; model/provider/prompt provenance, output and sink validation, policy-recorded provider substitution, typed tool contracts with caller/callee grants and policy-required human review, memory/retrieval privacy/retention/deletion/taint controls and secret redaction; replay returns recorded model/tool/retrieval/memory/review decisions or rejects a missing record. Interactive forms and generated code pass the ordinary compiler checks before execution; session manifests, transcripts, evaluated forms, syntax/core/MIR/source snapshots capture build-affecting state or mark nonhermeticity, and hot reload invalidates stale analysis/backend/runtime/package outputs. Reject live calls during replay, unvalidated trusted sinks, forbidden-profile eval, hidden interactive IO and stale reload artifacts. Dependencies: Domains supplies agent/workflow contracts, Schema supplies validators/migrations, Build consumes session inputs and invalidation, Auth supplies grants and review policy. Project work/token/call/time/retry allowances are removed admission requirements; actual provider billing/account limits remain external, and semantic failure/cancellation policy remains required. R8 mixed budget spans retain unresolved qualification in the family proposal.",
   :id
   "runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-distributedai-replay-and-interactive-execution",
   :before
   "Recorded nondeterminism, replay equality, no duplicated external effect, REPL grant denial",
   :collection :canonical-tasks}
  {:path "specs/runtime-workflow/tasks.md",
   :before-present? true,
   :field-path [:acceptance],
   :marker "runtime-implementation-tasks",
   :after-source-sha256
   "221b129f96156493c03e73e0ef3e8987f50425fcb15925c6a229144ea54539a1",
   :before-source-sha256
   "acf984517dbb6370c640a8d1fced94ddbc6799b86041746791959246da90c972",
   :after
   "Denial at actual service hook, redacted diagnostics and source-map preservation. R1/R11/R12: every authority-bearing action carries principal/package/deployment/artifact/source/effect/capability identity; deny by default and check both caller grant and tool/plugin contract; delegated handles are typed, scoped, provider-bound and revocable where supported, with use-after-revocation rejection; preserve grant/deny/delegate/revoke/audit records without secret disclosure and enforce deployment narrowing. Structured event/log/trace/metric/panic/replay bundles retain stable schemas/IDs, runtime/profile/target/source/generated-origin/artifact links, check/proof/replay references, redaction and remediation; sinks require grants, development services are marked, and sampling retains mandatory audit events without changing ordering, replay or safety. Reject ambient authority, ungranted sinks, secret/tainted/raw-memory leakage and lost required mappings/events. Dependencies: Auth supplies policy and grants, Lower supplies artifact/source maps, each runtime family supplies events, and testing/tooling/incident consumers validate bundles; these records do not grant authority or claim execution acceptance.",
   :id
   "runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-enforcement-and-observability-integration",
   :before
   "Denial at actual service hook, redacted diagnostics and source-map preservation",
   :collection :canonical-tasks}],
