    :entailment :proposed-source-qualified-interface,
    :acceptance
    "Denial at actual service hook, redacted diagnostics and source-map preservation. R1/R11/R12: every authority-bearing action carries principal/package/deployment/artifact/source/effect/capability identity; deny by default and check both caller grant and tool/plugin contract; delegated handles are typed, scoped, provider-bound and revocable where supported, with use-after-revocation rejection; preserve grant/deny/delegate/revoke/audit records without secret disclosure and enforce deployment narrowing. Structured event/log/trace/metric/panic/replay bundles retain stable schemas/IDs, runtime/profile/target/source/generated-origin/artifact links, check/proof/replay references, redaction and remediation; sinks require grants, development services are marked, and sampling retains mandatory audit events without changing ordering, replay or safety. Reject ambient authority, ungranted sinks, secret/tainted/raw-memory leakage and lost required mappings/events. Dependencies: Auth supplies policy and grants, Lower supplies artifact/source maps, each runtime family supplies events, and testing/tooling/incident consumers validate bundles; these records do not grant authority or claim execution acceptance.",
