    :entailment :proposed-source-qualified-interface,
    :acceptance
    "Recorded nondeterminism, replay equality, no duplicated external effect, REPL grant denial. R6/R7/R8/R9: topology/provider/event-log/state/message schemas; durable idempotency, timeout/retry/cancellation/failure/compensation records; migration or rejection of replay-incompatible code/topology/schema changes; model/provider/prompt provenance, output and sink validation, policy-recorded provider substitution, typed tool contracts with caller/callee grants and policy-required human review, memory/retrieval privacy/retention/deletion/taint controls and secret redaction; replay returns recorded model/tool/retrieval/memory/review decisions or rejects a missing record. Interactive forms and generated code pass the ordinary compiler checks before execution; session manifests, transcripts, evaluated forms, syntax/core/MIR/source snapshots capture build-affecting state or mark nonhermeticity, and hot reload invalidates stale analysis/backend/runtime/package outputs. Reject live calls during replay, unvalidated trusted sinks, forbidden-profile eval, hidden interactive IO and stale reload artifacts. Dependencies: Domains supplies agent/workflow contracts, Schema supplies validators/migrations, Build consumes session inputs and invalidation, Auth supplies grants and review policy. Project work/token/call/time/retry allowances are removed admission requirements; actual provider billing/account limits remain external, and semantic failure/cancellation policy remains required. R8 mixed budget spans retain unresolved qualification in the family proposal.",
    :qualification
    "Only the retained R1-R12 facets bind this interface. Other source contexts, historical decisions and additional task interfaces are conserved. This is task acceptance scope, not implementation acceptance.",
